  "question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project is centered around analyzing the data scientist job market. It aims to identify top-paying jobs and pinpoint in-demand skills within the field of data analytics. The focus is on uncovering where high demand intersects with high salaries, thereby optimizing job search efforts for individuals interested in data science roles.\n\nObjectives\n\n1. Identify top-paying data scientist jobs.\n2. Determine the most in-demand skills for data science positions.\n3. Analyze geographic and industry trends relating to job demand and salary.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Primary Users: Job seekers in the data science field.\n- Stakeholders: Career advisors, recruitment agencies, and companies seeking data scientists to understand market trends.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Job Market Analysis:\n   - Access and analyze data on job postings to identify highly-paid positions.\n   - Evaluate job titles and descriptions to extract in-demand skills.\n   - Use geo-location data to assess regional demand trends.\n\n2. Data Integration:\n   - Utilize a database schema incorporating company, skills, and job postings data.\n   - Ensure data accuracy and relevance through regular updates.\n\n3. Reporting & Insights:\n   - Generate reports detailing salary trends and skill demands.\n   - Provide visual insights into geographic and industry-specific trends.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Performance:\n   - The system should handle complex queries efficiently and provide insights in real-time.\n\n2. Scalability:\n   - Support an expanding dataset as new job postings and skill requirements emerge.\n\n3. Usability:\n   - Present data in a user-friendly format that is easily navigable for non-technical users.\n\n4. Security:\n   - Ensure data integrity and protect sensitive information from unauthorized access.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0211\nCREATE TABLE `companies` (\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `company_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `industry` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `website` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`company_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `job_postings` (\n  `job_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `company_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `job_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location_city` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location_state` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location_country` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `salary_min` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `salary_max` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `salary_currency` char(3) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `employment_type` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `posted_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_id`),\n  KEY `job_postings_ibfk_1` (`company_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `job_postings_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`company_id`) REFERENCES `companies` (`company_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `skills` (\n  `skill_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `skill_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `skill_category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`skill_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `skill_name` (`skill_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `job_skills` (\n  `job_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `skill_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `proficiency_level` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_id`,`skill_id`),\n  KEY `job_skills_ibfk_2` (`skill_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `job_skills_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`job_id`) REFERENCES `job_postings` (`job_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `job_skills_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`skill_id`) REFERENCES `skills` (`skill_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
